<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen firmer as Dow strengthens.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen firmer as Dow strengthens.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.30 a.m./2230 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2637.60  -35.40   DJIA  cl	7975.71  +52.73</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2644	-1   US 30yr cl	 6.55  steady</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.300  +0.030   Gold NY 318.25 Lon fix 319.75</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7337 (Tue 0.7355)   CRB Index cl   235.15   +0.64</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20069.41 -159.31   FTSE cl	 4899.30  +41.90</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   932.90   +1.15   NZSE40	  2471.58   +0.66</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 16)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen firmer as Dow strengthens, local market to steady. &quot;With the Dow being relatively strong and such a poor day yesterday we may be up a few points today,&quot; said one broker.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.25 (-.02), A$19.17 (+.002), A$6.17 (-.02), A$7.65 (steady)</p>
<p>*Wall Street stocks finished broadly higher with the Dow at an all-time high and Nasdaq hitting a ninth consecutive record close.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-7/16 (-2/16), BHP 27-1/8 (-5/16), WMC 22-5/8 (-7/16), National Australia Bank 71 (-1-11/16)</p>
<p>*Gold price was weaker. On LME, copper ended lower in volatile trade, with other metals generally weaker with copper.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
